    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_01ARm2SpERYc712ZkEjBfMhm",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "F74"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The Prime Minister's Scottish package (a joint offer to Holyrood made through Number 10 North and the Scotland Office, plus DWP devolution as localised employment support) is still only an offer, and its first real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers due in a couple of weeks.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S2:F15",
                  "S2:F33"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "The UK is not resting on the energy ceasefire President Trump announced, which still has no confirmed start date. It is tightening oil and LNG sanctions and speeding up air-defence deliveries for Ukraine's winter, and treats the ceasefire as unproven.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F13",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "S8:F27",
                  "S8:F85",
                  "S7:F25",
                  "S16:F92"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "The week's Record is almost entirely government statements of intent dated 11 to 16 October, so the outcomes that would show whether they hold are still ahead: a ceasefire start date, the meeting with the First Ministers, the Home Secretary's Fairford update and the 20 November UK-EU summit.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "L1",
                  "L2",
                  "F74"
                ],
                "text": "This week is best read as Andy Burnham setting out his early agenda. He has been Prime Minister only since 20 July, after nine years as Mayor of Greater Manchester that ended in June, and he still talks about his first week in office."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F93",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "L2"
                ],
                "text": "His domestic announcements share a former metro mayor's concern with the regions. He has created Number 10 North and wants Holyrood to work with it, offered Scotland DWP devolution as localised employment support, opened the Great British Railways headquarters in Derby, and announced £1 billion for new northern trains to be built there."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N1",
                  "S16:F83",
                  "S17:F82"
                ],
                "text": "For now the Scottish package is an offer, not a deal. The one concrete thing Holyrood has agreed in the Record is to match £10 million for two defence technical colleges, and the real test is the National Economic Council meeting with the First Ministers due in a couple of weeks."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "On Ukraine, the energy ceasefire President Trump announced still has no confirmed start date; Ukraine has said only that it will implement it once one is set."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "S2:F15",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "London is not waiting for it. A sanctions package now covers over 90% of Russia's oil-producing capacity, a maritime services ban on Russian LNG exports is to be fully implemented, and £10 million of a £45 million air-defence missile package is being speeded up for Ukraine's fifth winter under bombardment."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S3:F33",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "Ministers have also been told to draw up more sanctions, military aid and fiscal packages. On Ukraine the new government is continuing its predecessor's course and speeding it up, not changing direction."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "N3",
                  "S8:F27",
                  "S8:F85",
                  "S7:F25"
                ],
                "text": "One caution: almost everything here is the government describing its own intentions, and nothing in the Record is dated after 16 October. The dates to watch are the meeting with the First Ministers, the Home Secretary's update on RAF Fairford, and the 20 November UK-EU summit in Brussels, where Burnham wants a new food and farming deal."
              }
            ],
            "stories": []
          }
        }
      ],
